 "free": false,
 "audio_url": null,
 "note_en": "The particle 过 after a verb talks about experience: something has happened at least once in your life. 她坐过马车 \"she had ridden in a horse cart.\" The negative is 没…过: 没离开过县城 \"had never once left the county town.\" Note that 过 doesn't mean \"long ago\" and doesn't replace 了 — it's not about when something happened, but whether it ever did.",
